description "podman and an OCI runtime, which bootc shells out to for the image store every upgrade opens"

supports "debian" "ubuntu"

provides "container-runtime"

requires "build-environment"

// Measured 2026-09-04 on a machine installed by `tect install`: `bootc upgrade`
// died on `Upgrading composefs: Creating imgstorage: Initializing images: No
// such file or directory (os error 2)`, and the error is `execve` failing, not
// a missing directory. bootc keeps its composefs image store at
// `composefs/bootc/storage` and initialises a fresh one by *running* `podman
// images` in it — `podstorage.rs::CStorage::create` calls
// `Command::new(bootc_utils::podman_bin())`, and `podman_bin()` is the literal
// string `"podman"` unless `BOOTC_EXP_EXTERNAL_CONTAINER_TOOL` names something
// else. The base shipped skopeo and no podman, so there was nothing to exec.
//
// **So a deb bootc host needs podman on the installed machine, not just in the
// builder.** `quay.io/fedora/fedora-bootc:44` carries `podman-5.8.4` and
// `crun`, which is what made this a gap in this base rather than a bootc bug:
// the reference base has always had them and nothing here had ever run an
// upgrade to notice. That is also why it is a module rather than two more names
// on `bootc`'s package list — the dependency is real, it is bootc's, and
// `requires "container-runtime"` is how a repository is told so before it
// builds instead of a month later when an upgrade fails.
//
// `crun` and not `runc`: it is what Fedora's base uses, it is what podman
// defaults to on both families, and it is the smaller of the two. `crun-wasm`
// rides along in the same package and is not asked for.
provides "podman" "crun"

// Measured on both bases the same day: `podman` 5.8.6 with `crun` 1.28 on
// `debian:forky`, `podman` 5.7.0 with `crun` 1.21 on `ubuntu:26.04`.
packages "podman" "crun"
